bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    stage2_if_expr_result_join_untyped_match_payload_2026-11-07, 2, "2026-11-09 lane-p2-1 BLOCKED-EVIDENCE. Native repro CONFIRMED on stage2_new4.exe (built 2026-11-09 09:49, after the HIR join fix 81138a16f08 of 2026-11-07): test/fixtures/compiler/hir_untyped_if_result_subject/original.spl -> mir=2, bare variant Ok/Err ambiguous, subject at :17:11 has type unresolved. Interpreted HIR+MIR harness (new test/01_unit/compiler/50.mir/untyped_if_result_ctor_join_spec.spl, 7 cases: if/else, nested Err(if), elif chain, annotated control, same-module struct/enum decls, disagreeing-Ok negative) is GREEN on current source: probe shows the let local retains Result<[u8], text> produced by statements.spl binding_branch_join. So the source join is correct and the defect is a native-only divergence inside binding_branch_join/binding_block_value_type/binding_field_type under stage2 codegen. Missing: a stage2 rebuild carrying an eprint probe in binding_branch_join to see which arm returns unknown (C: had 4-8 GB free; native guard needs >= 8 GB), then fix that miscompile. No guess patch; jit_instantiator annotation kept."    native_build_cold_init_admission_wall_386s_2026-11-07, 0, "2026-11-09 lane-p2-1 BLOCKED-EVIDENCE. Reproduced natively: stage2_new4.exe native-build --entry-closure of a 30-line single-file entry with SIMPLE_SCV_INVENTORY_COLD_INIT=1 took 631 s wall, of which the build phases (parse..mir) took ~20 s (build-trace elapsed_ms=19542 at mir) -> ~610 s is admission, worse than the 386 s seed figure. Two costs: (1) source_authority.spl:242-246 widens cold inventory_roots to src+test+examples/10_tooling, and _compiler_inventory_refresh_observed_cost_v1 documents that a cold refresh REPLACES the inventory so its roots must cover the whole scope (the warm cursor then requires untracked_src/test digests); (2) scv_compile_snapshot_acquire_cost_v2 materialises every file of the selectors (src/lib,src/app,src/compiler,src/os) into build/scv/snapshots. Scoping either to the entry closure changes the inventory/snapshot authority contract (partial-scope cursor, per-family generations) - a design decision, not a local patch. Missing: owner design for per-root cold inventory caching + a phase cost profile (SIMPLE_INVENTORY_TRACE_ATTEMPT token run was killed by the disk guard at 290 s, C: 4-8 GB free)."    interp_private_names_selfhost_check_2026-11-09, 0, "2026-11-09 lane-p2-1 BLOCKED-EVIDENCE. Insertion point identified: module_import_resolution.spl named-import loop (after surface_declares_item_indexed) can reject a ModuleSurfaceCallable with is_public=false from a different-directory, non-test/** importer, mirroring seed check_private_use_names (module_loader.rs:616) + is_test_caller. Blockers: (a) 20.hir has no file I/O and no project-root handle, so the 20181-pair scripts/check/private_import_baseline.txt must be loaded by the driver and transported into HirLowering (new field + driver wiring); (b) native builds lower SCV snapshot paths (build/scv/snapshots/<rev>/...), so the repo-relative baseline key must strip that prefix or every baselined legacy pair becomes a hard error and the self-hosted bootstrap breaks; (c) proving (b) needs a stage2 rebuild + native closure build, not possible with C: at 4-8 GB free. Without (a)+(b) the check is a guess patch with bootstrap-break risk."
    stage2_if_expr_result_join_untyped_match_payload_2026-11-07, 0, "2026-11-07 OPEN; owner HIR lane5 / debug_truth with compiler owner for admitted native reproduction. PR7553 merged41d2785d3ee597f7e8f68c6f22aa7bea0c79bd4e adds regression only; no production fix. Native if/Result root cause remains UNDETERMINED; historical HIR-versus-native hypotheses are not a confirmed current diagnosis."
    stage2_if_expr_result_join_untyped_match_payload_2026-11-07, 1, "Unblock only after absolute SIMPLE_BIN is an admitted final compiler and coordinator supplies a 450-second outer process-tree watchdog: \"$SIMPLE_BIN\" test test/02_integration/compiler/hir/untyped_if_result_subject_cli_spec.spl --mode=interpreter. Three original/annotated/if-chain cases compile then run actual payloads, each compile120s/run10s. Runtime/native/docgen NOT_RUN. Evidence doc/08_tracking/bug/mir_untyped_if_expr_result_subject_2026-11-07.md and mirrored doc/06_spec/02_integration/compiler/hir/untyped_if_result_subject_cli_spec.md."
    stage2_if_expr_result_join_untyped_match_payload_2026-11-07, 3, "2026-11-11 opus-fix-lane FIX-IMPLEMENTED-VERIFICATION-PENDING. Root cause (native-only): binding_join_type dropped the whole if-join to untyped whenever one arm tail was unresolved, so under stage2 code_result lost its settled Result<[u8], text> even though the other arm carried it. Fix: statements.spl binding_join_type adopts the other arm when one arm is unresolved and the other is a Result settled by hir_const_type_settled (partial Results, non-Results, two unknowns and conflicting arms still stay unresolved); the binding_kind_type If/IfChain caller accepts it unchanged. Specs: test/01_unit/compiler/20.hir/binding_join_type_unresolved_arm_spec.spl (synthetic HirType, red 4/6 -> green 6/6), untyped_if_result_ctor_join_spec.spl +4 cases (11/11). Also made 50.mir module_lowering mir_lower_env_get pub (private-fn visibility error broke every MIR lowering spec on release). Remaining native check: rebuild stage2 and native-build test/fixtures/compiler/hir_untyped_if_result_subject/original.spl -> no bare Ok/Err ambiguity at :17:11; then drop the jit_instantiator annotation."
    stage2_if_expr_result_join_untyped_match_payload_2026-11-07, 4, "2026-11-12 opus-fix-lane (resumed from fable lane). Root cause (MIR, the half the 11-11 HIR fix left out): remember_merged_result_ctor_arm_type (src/compiler/50.mir/mir_lowering_stmts.spl) adopted a Result only from an already-typed arm; with every if/elif arm a bare untyped Ok/Err constructor the merge slot stayed untyped and `match r: case Ok(x)` failed as bare-variant ambiguous whenever another enum declared Ok/Err. Fix: lower_enum_construct_named tags each untyped Ok/Err ctor with a payload witness (retained local HIR type, expression type, declared non-generic field type, MIR Str fact; Infer/Error/Any refused) and remember_all_untyped_result_ctor_join owns Result<ok, err> only when every arm is such a ctor, both sides are present and each side agrees. Native A/B with Stage 2 built by the seed from the same tip (base 697173fae39f vs fix e52868126077): original/ifchain red(ambiguous)->green PASS, annotated green both, Ok-only arms stay red (missing side). Disagreeing Ok payloads ([u8] vs text) still refused by the pure-Simple compiler logic but ACCEPTED on seed-compiled Stage 2 because hir_types_equal([u8], text) returns true there (filed seed_tuple_pattern_bare_fieldless_variant_binds_hir_types_equal_true_2026-11-12: the seed binds bare fieldless variants in tuple patterns, so `case (Bool, Bool)` catches every pair). Spec untyped_if_result_ctor_join_spec gains a zero-MIR-functions vacuity guard (seed harness lowers 0 functions)."

